[2026-03-14T21:58:32.731Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013A2p5W2GcyTN2ZnzFYJ9Me","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. According to the documentation, it allows investigators to \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Investigation Approach\n\nThe framework emphasizes systematic investigation:\n1. Frame your inquiry as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form and support hypotheses with gathered data\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover *what* happened and *when*:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection and search\n\n**Explanatory Tools** reveal *why* events occurred:\n- Stack frames and control dependencies\n- Point descriptions with variable values\n- DOM element and React component inspection\n- Expression evaluation and logpoint analysis\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n- **Point**: A unique moment when a JS statement executes or significant event occurs\n- **Element**: A persistent DOM element reference independent of specific execution points\n\nThe documentation recommends using the Logpoint tool to track expression values across execution and the ControlDependency tool to understand event timing relationships."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cdd34ca-8e29-49de-a9ba-6b167a19810e","uuid":"9f694604-3585-4f62-8a1a-4f06d7dec44b","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. According to the documentation, it allows investigators to \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Investigation Approach\n\nThe framework emphasizes systematic investigation:\n1. Frame your inquiry as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form and support hypotheses with gathered data\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover *what* happened and *when*:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection and search\n\n**Explanatory Tools** reveal *why* events occurred:\n- Stack frames and control dependencies\n- Point descriptions with variable values\n- DOM element and React component inspection\n- Expression evaluation and logpoint analysis\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n- **Point**: A unique moment when a JS statement executes or significant event occurs\n- **Element**: A persistent DOM element reference independent of specific execution points\n\nThe documentation recommends using the Logpoint tool to track expression values across execution and the ControlDependency tool to understand event timing relationships.","durationMs":3248,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T21:58:35.331Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QLhFYqmrWRu24oGZT4EMqc","type":"tool_result","content":"# replay-cli\n\n**Description:** Use when the user wants help with Replay CLI commands for recording, uploading, managing recordings, or authentication. Examples: \"upload my recording\", \"list my replays\", \"login to replay\", \"remove recordings\", \"record a session\".\n\n**Instructions:**\n\nYou are helping the user with the Replay CLI tool. Here is the complete reference:\n\n### Installation\n\nInstall Replay CLI globally using your preferred package manager:\n\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n# or\nyarn add -g replayio\n# or\npnpm i -g replayio\n# or\nbun i -g replayio\n```\n\n### Authentication\n\nNavigate to https://app.replay.io settings page, create your API key and save the API key in the environment variable `REPLAY_API_KEY`.\n\n### Available Commands\n\n| Command              | Arguments    | Options                                                           |\n| -------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `info`               | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `list`               | –            | `--json`                                                          |\n| `login`              | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `logout`             | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `record`             | `[url]`      | –                                                                 |\n| `remove`             | `[ids...]`   | `-a`, `--all`                                                     |\n| `update`             | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `upload`             | `[ids...]`   | –                                                                 |\n| `upload-source-maps` | `<paths...>` | `-g`, `--group`, `-x`, `--extensions`, `-i`, `--ignore`, `--root` |\n| `help`               | –            | –                                                                 |\n\nPass `-h` or `--help` to any command for more info.\n\n### Command Details\n\n#### `replayio info`\n\nDisplays information about installed Replay dependencies including CLI version and Replay Browser info.\n\n#### `replayio list`\n\nLists all local recordings with their ID, host, date, duration, and status (Uploaded/Recorded).\n\n- `--json` - prints full list with details\n\n#### `replayio login`\n\nOpens browser to log in to your Replay account. Creates account if needed.\n\n#### `replayio logout`\n\nLogs out from Replay account. Does NOT invalidate API keys in environment variables.\n\n#### `replayio record [url]`\n\nLaunches Replay Browser and starts recording the given URL. Default URL is `about:blank`.\n\n- Recording continues until browser is closed\n- If not prompted differently, agent should upload just the main URL\n- Automatically checks for browser/CLI updates\n\n#### `replayio remove [ids...]`\n\nRemoves one or more recordings.\n\n- Without arguments: opens interactive menu to select recordings\n- With IDs: removes specified recordings\n- `-a`, `--all` - removes all local recordings\n\n#### `replayio update`\n\nUpdates the Replay Browser only. CLI updates are done via npm/yarn/pnpm/bun.\n\n#### `replayio upload [ids...]`\n\nUploads one or more recordings.\n\n- Without arguments: opens interactive menu to select recordings\n- With IDs: uploads specified recordings\n- Returns URL to view recording after upload\n\n#### `replayio upload-source-maps <paths...>`\n\nUploads source maps for a Workspace.\n\n- `-g`, `--group <name>` - group name (e.g., commit SHA or release version)\n- `-x`, `--extensions <exts>` - file extensions to process (default: \".js,.map\")\n- `-i`, `--ignore <pattern>` - ignore files matching pattern\n- `--root <dirname>` - base directory for relative paths\n\n#### `replayio help`\n\nDisplays all available commands and descriptions.\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n**Record and upload a session:**\n\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n# After recording, you'll be prompted to upload\n```\n\n**Upload a specific recording:**\nIf upload wasn't done automatically after recording, agent should upload the recording manually using the recording ID from previous step\n\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n**Run Replay MCP Server to debug your recored application**\nto install the MCP server in Claude, run the following command:\n\n```\nclaude --mcp-config \"{\n    \"mcpServers\": {\n      \"replay\": {\n        \"type\": \"http\",\n        \"url\": \"https://dispatch.replay.io/nut/mcp\",\n        \"headers\": {\n          \"Authorization\": \"${REPLAY_API_KEY}\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\"\n```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cdd34ca-8e29-49de-a9ba-6b167a19810e","uuid":"d559dd04-2f5a-4447-b5c9-ee2cdd9c6d48","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# replay-cli\n\n**Description:** Use when the user wants help with Replay CLI commands for recording, uploading, managing recordings, or authentication. Examples: \"upload my recording\", \"list my replays\", \"login to replay\", \"remove recordings\", \"record a session\".\n\n**Instructions:**\n\nYou are helping the user with the Replay CLI tool. Here is the complete reference:\n\n### Installation\n\nInstall Replay CLI globally using your preferred package manager:\n\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n# or\nyarn add -g replayio\n# or\npnpm i -g replayio\n# or\nbun i -g replayio\n```\n\n### Authentication\n\nNavigate to https://app.replay.io settings page, create your API key and save the API key in the environment variable `REPLAY_API_KEY`.\n\n### Available Commands\n\n| Command              | Arguments    | Options                                                           |\n| ----