eld.\n\nLet me look at the test to see what it's actually trying to do...\n\nThe test is checking that all property types display in the dropdown and that the title input is accessible. The current approach of clicking the title input to dismiss the dropdown causes the interception error because the dropdown visually blocks it. I'll update the test to use Escape or toggle the dropdown closed properly.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the real issue might be with how the overlay is positioned. If the relative container is creating a stacking context, the fixed overlay might not be escaping it properly. Let me check if the modal container has overflow clipping that's preventing the overlay from rendering outside its bounds.\n\nActually, I think the better approach here is to skip the overlay entirely and use a click-outside handler with useEffect and useRef instead.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1259,"cache_read_input_tokens":40429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1259,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cdd34ca-8e29-49de-a9ba-6b167a19810e","uuid":"0170620f-fbbc-43b2-abe7-849e955a3c1e"}
